#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/id #uuid "32bd6b27-e95d-5de4-941f-309eb0bc61f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4411" :question/problem "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046857/assets/90f675ec2a211b6157f040735d551d083c770ac33b5dbfcd74b3678b16d5df53.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-CB & =(A-C)B \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/id #uuid "3b1395b6-49c1-5e0d-ac94-c2d6fc242f6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4412" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046857/assets/de98e19bed31050fd07f9979f0428ed4eb90ce05eaff7ba4d19ea81bbd664422.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "7ab158e6-4222-5cab-88a0-85ce74a7d4b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4413" :question/problem "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\n- $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\n- $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "872dd646-4989-56ca-aa45-3be03e7a93a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326215} {:answer/id #uuid "975b5ecf-130c-53a8-8cbd-527d6a89dbbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326216} {:answer/id #uuid "609ad105-9e54-521c-bf94-40e110db9035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326217} {:answer/id #uuid "e083fbf5-d56d-55ba-bad2-26abc7ba2ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326218} {:answer/id #uuid "2c98481b-2e9e-5e9c-97bb-252adfc4799a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e083fbf5-d56d-55ba-bad2-26abc7ba2ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326218} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9d95c8c-acb6-5680-a4f6-8fdd7c25c381" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8441f0a-579a-53ac-9a6d-fa812952db44" :question/math-academy-id "q-130259" :question/problem "Calculate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daf48bcd-3e22-538c-a048-7768bf351c0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -9 & 24 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293647} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5e3af3-359c-573c-8659-8adb9a64f010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293648} {:answer/id #uuid "86895714-6b91-571c-afb5-3c9a38e025dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 & -21 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293649} {:answer/id #uuid "5c12bf6f-0686-5a12-a788-8b2b087181b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293650} {:answer/id #uuid "fab7f6ae-164e-50cf-95f9-81545d92e939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fab7f6ae-164e-50cf-95f9-81545d92e939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293651} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe195ede-7b12-52a3-aa15-6278ab312682" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0d357e4-9d79-5897-b810-6e18d8e35e77" :question/math-academy-id "q-130313" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b307c6c-b66a-5d39-8298-9e7eba80f467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284290} {:answer/id #uuid "84a1361a-1e8e-5442-b48f-b8c533733c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284291} {:answer/id #uuid "a73e9be0-a15c-5e95-8efa-ac9158db8bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284292} {:answer/id #uuid "8c675a0b-99ca-5086-8620-c9431c39b740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284293} {:answer/id #uuid "f031a871-3f8b-5f28-bf58-220ac920e602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b307c6c-b66a-5d39-8298-9e7eba80f467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284290} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d147b5f-6d58-5c16-b472-c51cdf38be30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e3975d8-0204-5147-a2bf-df4657a2f13f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130449" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $3\\times 3$ matrices, and  ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=A{I}_{3}B$\n- $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB$\n- ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $A{I}_{3}B=(A{I}_{3})B=AB.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB+A{I}_{3}=AB+A.$ However,  $AB+A\\ne AB,$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b40d0660-22b7-5681-b444-94fe6db6f44f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326222} {:answer/id #uuid "ef542b07-b133-5b47-a18f-987407074823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326223} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d209b9-4c23-5d22-a747-20ca777e3ba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326224} {:answer/id #uuid "0abd0e47-8eb5-592f-8345-2bb3da401382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326225} {:answer/id #uuid "77b21f47-b2e2-5468-8675-2b6e8dd3952b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef542b07-b133-5b47-a18f-987407074823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326223} :answer-field/id #uuid "03fba02b-8aa8-5f79-a31b-58f220489b4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3b611f4-2cbe-5a36-a4d2-5f484cd27e51" :question/math-academy-id "q-130463" :question/problem "Given that $A$ and $B$  are $8\\times 8$ matrices,  and ${I}_{8}$ is the $8\\times 8$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A$\n- $AB=BA$\n- $A\\cdot 2{I}_{8}=2A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot 2{I}_{8} & =A({I}_{8}+{I}_{8}) \\\\  & =A{I}_{8}+A{I}_{8} \\\\  & =A+A \\\\  & =2A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statements I  and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6a1b6fa-78d9-54be-82fa-1d304999af3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326229} {:answer/id #uuid "1382838b-4854-5d6b-a025-e4ee7faa566b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1382838b-4854-5d6b-a025-e4ee7faa566b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326230} :answer-field/id #uuid "421df267-be95-5f95-9bd9-7045920adc1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efdf4e61-5da9-5844-b463-281661c8a3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efdf4e61-5da9-5844-b463-281661c8a3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326232} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e044cac-199f-5a2b-8ce8-2c7a10847b48" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9357c1ec-d42b-510d-af03-fc9daf963ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9357c1ec-d42b-510d-af03-fc9daf963ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326234} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab75e2d2-9656-5623-94bd-b51c72784e67" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9054c2bb-e8ec-5523-9043-ab29e0bfc4bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-275515" :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $-2$ |  |\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =A{I}_{3} \\\\  & =A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6906ccdb-67bf-5601-96ad-3fad8344c524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6906ccdb-67bf-5601-96ad-3fad8344c524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284319} :answer-field/id #uuid "79136c64-d827-567e-8129-842c22759199" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2babf67-567f-5287-8719-752fb496e896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2babf67-567f-5287-8719-752fb496e896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284321} :answer-field/id #uuid "7850a0bc-bc03-5bae-bd60-9696e52880fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b93b47e-9d99-52be-bd00-730a53fe6261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b93b47e-9d99-52be-bd00-730a53fe6261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284323} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd042ce3-79ce-5510-b444-5bc6e8cfe954" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3c06a29-7a18-544d-bf9a-8bad4341bcc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-319886" :question/problem "Evaluate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC+BC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $3$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88227a76-b8b0-5e39-aeb0-8f18f6ee79f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88227a76-b8b0-5e39-aeb0-8f18f6ee79f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326237} :answer-field/id #uuid "375be16f-00ec-5c9b-886b-0d097b6c8a65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bab3564a-8229-51a4-88d3-91abed9958e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bab3564a-8229-51a4-88d3-91abed9958e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326239} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b5a142-868b-5a45-97a7-3d577f2f492b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a75080eb-0fec-5b12-aa8e-ce21f3a61729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a75080eb-0fec-5b12-aa8e-ce21f3a61729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326241} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae08e9c-92e2-5d57-9a69-ee051437b00b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cde2051-0eec-5f75-88ad-b1739f5a1e2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-319890" :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3af8c0a-9e31-5da6-8775-ecd749d53ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3af8c0a-9e31-5da6-8775-ecd749d53ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326244} :answer-field/id #uuid "a36a705b-af7b-5a9a-890b-4b248a830293" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bee03a72-c06e-5c6a-a587-bdf1c436fab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bee03a72-c06e-5c6a-a587-bdf1c436fab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326246} :answer-field/id #uuid "a29f0bde-1921-5989-ae31-c2c4919ee15b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e3d4e7e-32c4-5ccb-af15-afbabd9363ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e3d4e7e-32c4-5ccb-af15-afbabd9363ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326248} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8620d7e-6b6c-5cd6-bfa9-4d06cf95cb2f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d048e189-ed2b-5974-bb9f-09412e2f82ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d048e189-ed2b-5974-bb9f-09412e2f82ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326250} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d8c945b-fb4b-5091-9920-1a5eb9264c8b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b97b0d1e-9082-51dd-b8cd-b8799d1082f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-319917" :question/problem "Calculate $CB-CA$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $CB-CA=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nCB-CA=C(B-A).\n$$\n\nSo, compute $B-A$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-3{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB-CA & =C(B-A) \\\\  & =C(-3{I}_{3}) \\\\  & =-3C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cbbffd2-c482-515d-8bcc-7e95b417ee3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cbbffd2-c482-515d-8bcc-7e95b417ee3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293661} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc6da346-ec1e-523a-acd9-74dfb0bb9e66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "289107a9-561a-5bdd-9f05-49dfec32a3b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "289107a9-561a-5bdd-9f05-49dfec32a3b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293663} :answer-field/id #uuid "76592d76-ccfa-56a1-9df0-9382c809d481" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e617169-2a55-53ef-9dc0-d411029e0141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e617169-2a55-53ef-9dc0-d411029e0141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293665} :answer-field/id #uuid "e953a819-9007-5b5b-ac21-e054240b488e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "155f2f4f-9651-51d7-980e-63b64b381dae" :question/math-academy-id "q-319938" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-65 \\\\ 13 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6940fca4-92f2-5cba-9deb-f531c54a0aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6940fca4-92f2-5cba-9deb-f531c54a0aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326253} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe55f9b-5f6e-571e-ba5e-3ad49dada07b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7947acc9-7664-52a2-bd7e-8922f97e9f2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "136" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7947acc9-7664-52a2-bd7e-8922f97e9f2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "136" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326255} :answer-field/id #uuid "59faf82c-5de7-5533-adad-187c159602df" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9493362-0810-5236-a3c8-f24f6e1eb12e" :question/math-academy-id "q-320026" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $4$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 34\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 34\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-58 & 136\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aebb4360-8326-58cc-a7ca-816d512eec3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113806} {:answer/id #uuid "ef45baf8-81df-5edc-9d1e-1ffb3358dcbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113807} {:answer/id #uuid "fc44e8aa-6f75-5291-a8dc-77e56b4a3328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113808} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6a475f-9fef-5ea6-9665-a0ab5dbd5770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113809} {:answer/id #uuid "6a24c934-0494-5b2e-aa71-129d78fcdbcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc44e8aa-6f75-5291-a8dc-77e56b4a3328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113808} :answer-field/id #uuid "969084eb-bca2-5ea0-bef4-60a97533d6d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d05ca169-7c67-546f-9f08-0fce1486794c" :question/math-academy-id "q-41785" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "678b2272-7810-5f56-a6ac-c62a10f854fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 18 & 9 \\\\ 21 & 7 & -42 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284350} {:answer/id #uuid "158cb1d4-a4f8-5487-99e1-767acc3a676f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284351} {:answer/id #uuid "761fb85b-7392-51f2-a63e-085c9a729140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 42 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284352} {:answer/id #uuid "881f57bb-479b-5b8e-8d7f-0c549e81b862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 9 & -42 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284353} {:answer/id #uuid "087bc156-bdfb-592d-896a-4cca3f807665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158cb1d4-a4f8-5487-99e1-767acc3a676f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284351} :answer-field/id #uuid "e140af37-5d21-52b2-9992-47ed85fb2f2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "638edf80-8d70-51f1-a06b-07cfe064f004" :question/math-academy-id "q-42001" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11f9e2a-ed97-5892-b658-f32e3c6b3291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113866} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6d062e-bc5c-536f-95e3-3119d32f14f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113867} {:answer/id #uuid "020544b6-6ee9-557b-9286-6492929bdd13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113868} {:answer/id #uuid "3d590048-cce3-5884-bde5-8be926e7dd54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113869} {:answer/id #uuid "7b35efad-7299-53b3-b06f-d3b8164ad052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd6d062e-bc5c-536f-95e3-3119d32f14f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113867} :answer-field/id #uuid "35146e5c-364f-5229-9c30-59d0b677108a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "174631dd-f119-50e8-bf7b-ac669b330d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-42266" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $(A+B)C=AC+BC$\n- $AB=BA$\n- $A(BC)=(BA)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC)=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edd17d48-dd87-53f2-b774-01ce8ca6444d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326258} {:answer/id #uuid "d13e5406-5440-52e9-bc60-db67a32ac193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326259} {:answer/id #uuid "0fdcd809-9310-5bfd-b3f9-be1b94c23554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326260} {:answer/id #uuid "1b181350-30ae-5258-b164-1e8042facc95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326261} {:answer/id #uuid "d436b3a4-5507-5bba-a181-9f08e3ce96ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edd17d48-dd87-53f2-b774-01ce8ca6444d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326258} :answer-field/id #uuid "64901020-c8d1-535a-83a6-522370373620" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be6e8e19-7022-5ded-a9f9-f8652f73cf31" :question/math-academy-id "q-42267" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $5\\times 5$ matrices, and  ${I}_{5}$ is the $5\\times 5$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=BA$\n- $A(B+C)=AB+AC$\n- $B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B=B.$\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6eb0d88-2fd2-52de-91bc-9af61b9158cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326265} {:answer/id #uuid "924594b4-d799-5e7c-a60f-20c7a2a4171f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326266} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4794d1-6bd6-5787-9028-04a689758f60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326267} {:answer/id #uuid "fde2a93d-c6f0-5365-b631-52802265652a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326268} {:answer/id #uuid "fc37606b-7354-5384-9aca-4d36dd8a52f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "924594b4-d799-5e7c-a60f-20c7a2a4171f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326266} :answer-field/id #uuid "fadd03e5-8730-58cb-8eaa-be2b9f7fc337" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ec9156e-6a13-5769-a47f-7384d9da375e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75662" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A(B+C)=AC+AB$\n- $A(BC)=(BA)C$\n- $AB=BA$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\nA(B+C)=AB+AC=AC+AB\n$$\n\n since matrix addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC)=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}]}
